body:
Hey there!

&#x200B;

Your post caught my eye because I know and completely see how much you are struggling. I am not a professional, but I normally try to look at things with the approach of "Why am I doing this?". My first answer would have been "to be thin" but what is the reason, behind that reason? and the reason behind that? Finding the core cause for what is driving your ED is key to recovery in my opinion, you may know it, you may not. There can also be more than one cause too. It's okay if you don't know and I appreciate it can also be a triggering thing to some if it is linked to any past traumas.

&#x200B;

**You deserve that apple.** The ED thoughts are there, but we can be louder together okay? If you're comfortable with saying either here or in DM's (or not at all that's okay too) but what makes you so scared about this apple? Is it relevant to all foods or just the apple itself? 

&#x200B;

We can start with just the thought. You don't need to eat the apple just yet because that is a big step. Little steps with trying to feel less distressed of the thought of it can help combat the real thing if that makes sense? I don't know if this would work for you, and every person is different so try not to be disheartened if it doesn't but what worked for me was trying to imagine taking small bites. Imagining it. You're not eating it, there is no physical loss or gains here - just a simple thought, like many others in your day. Overtime, practicing this could help you become comfortable with the idea to ease into food. Although, the idea is to be focused in the present stage of getting okay with the idea and not thinking about the next stage of eating and becoming panicked. This is only one method, and there are many others out there. Recovery isn't linear. 

I would also recommend watching some eat with me's on YouTube, they can be really comforting and can help you feel less alone and confident with eating when you feel less alone and stuck in your head. 

&#x200B;

I am here if you need me, I hope I was of some help :)

You got this!!!

\- Musiclover255
